==English==

===Etymology===
{{blend|en|Bronck|-'s}}. After immigrant settler {{w|lang=en|Jonas Bronck}} (1600–1643) of [[New Netherlands]] onto the peninsula north of Manhattan Island.
* {{sense|region}} Originally ''{{l|en|Bronck's Land}}'', the land in the region settled by Jonas Bronck.
* {{sense|river}} Originally ''{{l|en|Bronck's River}}'', a river bordering the region settled by Jonas Bronck.

